  "reads": [
    "The same server, the same durations, three seeds: S = 20, 24, 46. The reported figure is the minimum the methodology asks for, 20.",
    "The spread is 26 streams, a factor of 2.3. That is the dominant source of uncertainty in every capacity number this project has published, and it was invisible until a run used more than one seed.",
    "It is larger than the fixed-versus-ragged difference published on 2026-09-14 (42 against 59, 17 streams, one seed each), so that comparison does not support the price it was used to state. Withdrawn; see the amendment in docs/why-fixed-shape-padding-works.md.",
    "Every rung that failed did so as UNSTABLE, never on latency: the warm-up p95 stopped settling within 10% while the last passing rung on each seed sat at 196-267 ms against a 310 ms budget. Consistent with the shorter runs, and the reading spread is what separates a passing rung from a failing one.",
    "Seed 20260916 reached 46 and seed 20260914 stopped at 20 on a server that did not change between them. Why the seed moves the answer this much is not established here and is the most important open question about this harness."
  ]
